            <div xml:id="d868">

                <pb facs="0923" n="911" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg911"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.5561/72: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-11-21T17:00:00+03:00">November 21, 1941—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 22—10:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1959. Department’s 1195, November 7, 11 a.m.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d868-f1"/> In
                    a note dated November 20 and received today the Foreign Office states in
                    substance that the Soviet Government will permit an Assistant Naval Attaché of
                    the Embassy to remain in Archangel. It adds however that in consideration of the
                    military situation the authorities deem it inexpedient to allow an Assistant
                    Naval Attaché to be stationed at one of the Black Sea ports at present and that
                    decision on this matter must therefore be postponed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
